┌ Warning: `energy_source_tags` with `turbconv: prognostic_edmfx`: the eddy diffusion moves the tags as passive tracers, while it moves `ρe_tot` in enthalpy form. The difference goes to `e_src_res`.
┌ Warning: `energy_source_tags` tag `mp` lists `microphysics`, which cannot contribute under NonEquilibriumMicrophysics1M. Only 0-moment microphysics changes `ρe_tot`. The other schemes move water between species, and the energy leaves with sedimentation, which the tags follow as transport. Note `moist` and `all` both expand to include `microphysics`.
┌ Warning: `energy_source_tags` tag `new_strat` lists `precipitation`, which cannot contribute to a source tag. It is the sedimentation of precipitating species, which moves energy between levels rather than adding it. Where water sediments, the tags follow it as transport instead, so nothing is credited to `precipitation`. The `energy_tracers` family does attribute it. Under 0-moment microphysics, rain leaves through `microphysics` instead. Note `moist` and `all` both expand to include `precipitation`.
┌ Warning: `energy_source_tags` tag `new_strat` lists `microphysics`, which cannot contribute under NonEquilibriumMicrophysics1M. Only 0-moment microphysics changes `ρe_tot`. The other schemes move water between species, and the energy leaves with sedimentation, which the tags follow as transport. Note `moist` and `all` both expand to include `microphysics`.
┌ Warning: `energy_source_tags` tag `new_tropo` lists `precipitation`, which cannot contribute to a source tag. It is the sedimentation of precipitating species, which moves energy between levels rather than adding it. Where water sediments, the tags follow it as transport instead, so nothing is credited to `precipitation`. The `energy_tracers` family does attribute it. Under 0-moment microphysics, rain leaves through `microphysics` instead. Note `moist` and `all` both expand to include `precipitation`.
┌ Warning: `energy_source_tags` tag `new_tropo` lists `microphysics`, which cannot contribute under NonEquilibriumMicrophysics1M. Only 0-moment microphysics changes `ρe_tot`. The other schemes move water between species, and the energy leaves with sedimentation, which the tags follow as transport. Note `moist` and `all` both expand to include `microphysics`.
┌ Warning: `energy_process_record` lists `microphysics`, which records nothing under NonEquilibriumMicrophysics1M. Only 0-moment microphysics changes `ρe_tot` and `ρq_tot`. The other schemes move water between species, so this record stays zero, which reads the same as a process that did nothing. Their rain-out is in the `precipitation` record.

